      "writtenOn": "2026-06-02T09:38:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That means the construct result type is not one of the structs rebuilt by this transform. The `struct_to_original` map is only needed when a struct was rewritten and the row-major member decoration was stripped from the new struct. In that case, the original struct lets us recover which members were row-major. If there is no original struct entry, there is no stripped row-major metadata to recover, so the existing type-difference check is sufficient.",
      "parentUuid": "2aca0ff8_cd530bcb",
      "revId": "4980e21bb32ae66e5b91e95117b467fa065eb411",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
